## 64 bits natives for Windows platform ##
Running on an 64 bits windows with the 32 bits JDK (e.g. Java Chrome Plugin for Windows only) implies that _64 bits_ native libraries must be loaded on the system. Therefore 64 bits native libraries like "jinput-dx8_64.dll" must be found in the project/resources/properties/Windows/all/natives and _not_ ../Windows/amd64/natives. This is because a 32 bits compiler will not look into amd64 folder to add the natives to the .jar.
This concern does not involve Mac OS and other Unix platforms which cannot run 32 bits JDK on 64 bits machines.